vdr-plugin-epg2vdr (1.1.0-0yavdr0~trusty) trusty; urgency=medium
    Caution: this new version is not compatible with epgd < 1.1.0
    To upgrade your systems the following procedure is recommended:
    1) Start all machines running vdr-plugin-epg2vdr
    2) Stop vdr on all machines
    3) Stop epgd (from package vdr-epg-daemon)
    4) Drop all tables used by epg2vdr (e.g. by running "sudo epgd-tool -drop-all")
    5) Update epgd (vdr-epg-daemon) to version 1.1.0 and read the changelog and README
    6) Start epgd
    7) Start epghttpd (if needed)
    8) Update vdr-plugin-epg2vdr and vdr-plugin-scraper2vdr on all machines to version >= 1.1.0
    9) delete /var/cache/epg.data and the folder /var/cache/vdr/plugins/scraper2vdr
    10) After the initial data update of epgd has finished, start your VDRs again
    

